---
import PortfolioLayout from '../layouts/PortfolioLayout.astro';
import profile from '../data/profile.json';
import now from '../data/now.json';
---

<PortfolioLayout
	title="About | Ritik Sharma"
	description="A little about Ritik Sharma: Python backend engineer, reader, foreign-film fan, teammate, and student of how LLMs work."
>
	<header class="page-intro">
		<p class="eyebrow">A little more than a job title</p>
		<h1>Curious about how things work.</h1>
		<p>I’m Ritik Sharma, a Python backend developer in {profile.location}. I like understanding what happens beneath the surface, then explaining what I learn in plain language.</p>
	</header>

	<div class="about-columns">
		<div class="about-prose">
			<p>At work, I build APIs and backend services with Python. I enjoy working with a team when we have a clear plan, can share context, and move through the work together.</p>
			<p>Lately, I’ve been trying to build a language model from scratch. I’ve only just started, and that’s the point: I want to understand the inner workings instead of treating the model as a black box. I’m writing about the questions and discoveries as I go.</p>
			<p>Away from code, I enjoy books and foreign films.</p>
			<p>This site is where I keep both sides: the systems I’ve worked on and the things I’m still figuring out.</p>
		</div>
		<aside class="about-aside" aria-labelledby="current-heading">
			<h2 id="current-heading">On my desk lately</h2>
			<ul>
				{now.currentlyExploring.map((item) => <li>{item}</li>)}
				<li>Books and foreign films</li>
			</ul>
		</aside>
	</div>
</PortfolioLayout>
